{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions","id":777740,"title":"Can Pan Have Scions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-01T07:11:52-08:00","id":777740,"title":"Can Pan Have Scions?","content":"After reading through Hero and Demigod, there are examples of Gods and Titans switching sides and becoming recognized as one or the other. For example, the Furies are technically Titanspawn, but are now identified as Goddesses. Conversely the Minotaur were created by Poseidon, but are now regarded as Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> <br /> So it gets a bit confusing as to what makes one a creation of the Gods and the Titans.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pan was once a member of the Dodekatheon and was a God of love and fertility. After he joined the Titans, however, he's now considered a demon. But is that just a label the pantheons slapped on him, or does he still have the potential to create Scions of his own?<br /> <br /> I was interested in trying to make a Scion of Pan, but I wasn't sure if that was possible, given his current status listed in Demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T08:25:07-08:00","id":777771,"title":"","content":"Short answer: Probably, if you bend the rules a bit.<br /> <br /> Longer answer: Technically, Pan wouldn't be capable of siring Scions the way a God or Greater Titan could due to the fact that he has &quot;only&quot; a Legend Rating of 8. This marks him a s a demigod or a very minor god, able to sire supernatural creatures with fellow being with a Legend Rating, but no Scions. Only beings with a Legend of 9 or higher can pass their Ichor on to offsprings that come from an union with a mortal partner. <br /> <br /> Now, as we all know, Scion is heavily imbalanced and has a metric ton of design flaws, so I'd be all for bending this rule a little, allowing Pan to actually father Scions the way other Gods do. The real trouble is: He wouldn't have anything associated either. Gods only have their Pantheons Special Purview associated automatically. Everything else follows different rules. To have an Epic Attribute associated with you, you need to have it at godly levels, which is 8 or higher. Purviews are even bigger, since you need to be able to use the Avatar Form of any Purview you want to have associated with you.Again, we could bend those rules in Pan's favor and give him the following traits: <br /> <br /> Associated Attributes: Charisma, Manipulation<br /> Associated Purviews: Animal (Goat), Arete, Chaos, Fertility","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T09:01:00-08:00","id":777785,"title":"","content":"However, demigod scions can sire/birth children who can be scions of their divine grandparent. So, any children of pan from a mortal might be a scion of his divine parent. Hermes, if I remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T09:58:22-08:00","id":777802,"title":"","content":"True, but that requires the Godparent (and a God who has Magic on an appropriate level) to adopt said child willingly. Or, you know, a Titan to snatch them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T12:29:27-08:00","id":777852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=777802#post777802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but that requires the Godparent (and a God who has Magic on an appropriate level) to adopt said child willingly. Or, you know, a Titan to snatch them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no, according to the books. It ain't the same as adopting a latent scion from another god, the children of Scions and lesser gods (legend 9-11) count as scions of those being's Legend 12 divine parent. So children of Pan should count as visitation scions of Hermes for atributes &amp; purviews, unless <b>outright negated</b> by the god himself, case in which they would become fair game for adoption by other deities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T12:39:15-08:00","id":777857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=777802#post777802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or, you know, a Titan to snatch them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually that's something else that confused me. If I remember correctly, the book states that the Scion's parent has to openly disown the Scion before they receive their visitation, then they're available to adopt. Yet Kane Taoka is registered as a Scion of Amaterasu and Mikaboshi.<br /> <br /> I highly doubt the Goddess of the Sun is going to tell the Titan of Darkness that he can have her kid. So how did this work out? Did Mikaboshi just take the role of an emissary for Amaterasu to awaken Kane's power, then gave him birthrights of his own making?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T17:31:09-08:00","id":777987,"title":"","content":"Kane was never formally disowned by Amaterasu so he couldn't be officially adopted by Mikaboshi... which is why it took a while for his band to discover his true loyalties. However, all of his boons and relics were given to him by Mikaboshi... even though he didn't favor the Purviews. Just because one favors certain Purviews, Skills and Attributes from their divine parent, it doesn't mean that the character has to learn them... just that they would have an easier time doing so if they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T18:47:19-08:00","id":778024,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but you'd think Amaterasu would be at least curious why a Scion she decided not to visit suddenly ichored up and is now wielding her Purviews. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, I haven't ordered God yet, so please no major spoilers regarding The Long Road's plot.<br /> <br /> <br /> If all it takes is a bit of experience points to make Pan a viable parent, then it doesn't sound too difficult to tweak him into such. But something you said earlier about Titans also being able to pass on their Ichor has me intrigued. Can the Titans produce Scions, too?<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't see why not since the Gods did come from them, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-01-2015, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T07:43:38-08:00","id":778312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=778024#post778024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but you'd think Amaterasu would be at least curious why a Scion she decided not to visit suddenly ichored up and is now wielding her Purviews. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, I haven't ordered God yet, so please no major spoilers regarding The Long Road's plot.<br /> <br /> <br /> If all it takes is a bit of experience points to make Pan a viable parent, then it doesn't sound too difficult to tweak him into such. But something you said earlier about Titans also being able to pass on their Ichor has me intrigued. Can the Titans produce Scions, too?<br /> <br /> I mean, I don't see why not since the Gods did come from them, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not 100% sure either way, i think the subject might be somewhat adressed in a SAS, Seeds of Tomorrow, or either Scion: God or the Companion, can't say for sure. And about the Titans and gods, it might be more precise to say that certain peculiar avatar mutated into gods through interaction with human imagination and Fate, setting the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> So <b>it might</b> be justifiable to argument that Gods generate scions and Titans do not due in part to this deeper connection, if any such a explanation is required, canon or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T08:28:01-08:00","id":778337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=777857#post777857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually that's something else that confused me. If I remember correctly, the book states that the Scion's parent has to openly disown the Scion before they receive their visitation, then they're available to adopt. Yet Kane Taoka is registered as a Scion of Amaterasu and Mikaboshi.<br /> <br /> I highly doubt the Goddess of the Sun is going to tell the Titan of Darkness that he can have her kid. So how did this work out? Did Mikaboshi just take the role of an emissary for Amaterasu to awaken Kane's power, then gave him birthrights of his own making?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have my book with me, but I really want to say that Hero explicitly notes that Titans can adopt Scions without their Godly parent's permission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T08:48:06-08:00","id":778349,"title":"","content":"That is correct Mockery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:21:12-08:00","id":778555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=778349#post778349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is correct Mockery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite - they can be visited and converted to their cause by Titans, not quite adopted without permission.<br /> Otherwise why would Kane Taoka be a Scion of Amaterasu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:43:26-08:00","id":778570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=778555#post778555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite - they can be visited and converted to their cause by Titans, not quite adopted without permission.<br /> Otherwise why would Kane Taoka be a Scion of Amaterasu?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, the closest I was able to find was the book saying an emissary of their parent can work to. They don't need to meet face to face with the God who spawned them. Which means that Mikaboshi could have arrived, told him he was a Scion, and that's how his power was awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T15:37:25-08:00","id":778639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=778570#post778570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, the closest I was able to find was the book saying an emissary of their parent can work to. They don't need to meet face to face with the God who spawned them. Which means that Mikaboshi could have arrived, told him he was a Scion, and that's how his power was awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Told him he was a scion of <b>Amaterasu</b> - the revelation of divine progenitor and Taoka's reaction to his mother's absence/omission are clearly still there as elements of the visitation even though twisted as it is by Mikaboshi hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:53:02-08:00","id":779200,"title":"","content":"Scion story Seeds of Tomorrow has a Scion of Pan in it but doesn't say in black and white whether he was adopted or conceived by Pan. I would use the argument that &quot;it's your game, you make the rules.&quot; Things go out the window when Scions of John Henry start turning up anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4662-xanbai","name":"Xanbai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T16:23:19-08:00","id":779347,"title":"","content":"Which book is that in? At present, I have Hero and Demigod. I'm planning to get God and Companion this month. Undecided on Ragnarok, yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T09:54:35-08:00","id":779898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=779347#post779347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which book is that in? At present, I have Hero and Demigod. I'm planning to get God and Companion this month. Undecided on Ragnarok, yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking to me, the Scion of Pan is in a story not in a book, it's one of those SAS stories (Seeds of Tomorrow as mentioned). The ones that give you an entire adventure to run. Scions of John Henry are in Scion Companion. Seeds of Tomorrow actually uses stuff from Scion Companion but I don't believe Pan is mentioned in the book.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Ragnarok, I would get it as it's a great expansion for the Norse coming with an entire three tier spanning story (From Hero to Demigod to God) all about the end of the world. Though it doesn't need to be played as the end of the world, you can pick and choose elements from it to put into a non end of the world story. The God tier part actually works well for the Titan Wars, you'll know what I'm talking about when you get Scion God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4662,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4662-xanbai","user":"Xanbai","date":". 12-04-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4662-xanbai","name":"Xanbai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T10:30:19-08:00","id":779929,"title":"","content":"Ragnarok also has two new purviews, if that helps. Illusion and Frost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:45:02-08:00","id":779991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanbai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=779898#post779898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're talking to me, the Scion of Pan is in a story not in a book, it's one of those SAS stories (Seeds of Tomorrow as mentioned). The ones that give you an entire adventure to run. Scions of John Henry are in Scion Companion. Seeds of Tomorrow actually uses stuff from Scion Companion but I don't believe Pan is mentioned in the book.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Ragnarok, I would get it as it's a great expansion for the Norse coming with an entire three tier spanning story (From Hero to Demigod to God) all about the end of the world. Though it doesn't need to be played as the end of the world, you can pick and choose elements from it to put into a non end of the world story. The God tier part actually works well for the Titan Wars, you'll know what I'm talking about when you get Scion God.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, I was asking where do I find &quot;Seeds of Tomorrow,&quot; whether or not it was included in one of the books or if it's a downloaded story like Liberty Road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:14:56-08:00","id":780024,"title":"","content":"Pan's Father was Hermes. Grandpa might give a Scion of Pan a visitation in order to both protect the scion and fight off Pan and his corrupted minions. Also, Apollo might realize he acted like a jerk and give a Scion of Pan a visitation, same motives, but more weighted to fighting off Pan's plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T15:06:00-08:00","id":780162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=779991#post779991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, I was asking where do I find &quot;Seeds of Tomorrow,&quot; whether or not it was included in one of the books or if it's a downloaded story like Liberty Road.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a downloaded story like Liberty Road, best bet is DriveThruRPG where it's about 5 quid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4662-xanbai","name":"Xanbai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T17:07:36-08:00","id":780240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=780024#post780024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pan's Father was Hermes. Grandpa might give a Scion of Pan a visitation in order to both protect the scion and fight off Pan and his corrupted minions. Also, Apollo might realize he acted like a jerk and give a Scion of Pan a visitation, same motives, but more weighted to fighting off Pan's plots.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hah, the Dodekatheon feeling remorse for their emotional outbursts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T02:16:08-08:00","id":780455,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I would rewrite Pan as a normal god who can have his own Scions. The Legend 9 requirement is needlessly restrictive. I would put him in the same category as Thanatos, Hypnos, Nyx and such : outsiders from the Olympians. Allows for power struggles and alliances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 12-05-2015, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:34:45-08:00","id":780498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=780455#post780455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I would rewrite Pan as a normal god who can have his own Scions. The Legend 12 requirement is needlessly restrictive. I would put him in the same category as Thanatos, Hypnos, Nyx and such : outsiders from the Olympians. Allows for power struggles and alliances.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What's even more confusing is his backstory says he's a god, yet his Legend is 8, which implies he's a demigod. I suppose it could have dropped after he left the Dodekatheon, but unlike them, he stayed behind in the world and took the form of Satan, so he's had thousands of years to rebuild his power.<br /> <br /> <br /> If there's one thing I've learned from the White Wolf community, it's that the books are more like guidelines than actual set in stone mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T04:54:15-08:00","id":780506,"title":"","content":"Plus, Legend 8 for Pan is really low. Ragnar\u00f6k has write-ups for gods like Forsetti or Bragi, and design them as viable parents, but there's no way Pan should be less 'famous' than them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T07:39:44-08:00","id":780549,"title":"","content":"Pan was, IIRC, considered quite potent in his particular purviews among the Greek gods. He didn't appear in most of their stories because he was considered so ugly but he had some pretty solid power. His name is at the root of the word 'panic' and his cries had scattered Titanspawn during the Titanomachy. That's some fairly serious oomph. And Pan was associated with a lot of things, for all that shepherds, fields and glens may not be as impressive as the entirety of the sky or war or such. Pan should certainly stand around the likes of Forsetti and Bragi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T07:42:11-08:00","id":780551,"title":"","content":"If anything, he could also be a solid five points guide. For a Scion of Dionysus or Hermes, most likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T09:53:38-08:00","id":780594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=780240#post780240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Hah, the Dodekatheon feeling remorse for their emotional outbursts!</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Apollo and Hermes were unpredictable in the ancient Myths, and Hermes often came close to a Humane moral outlook in his later actions. If any two male Olympians could feel regret and act well on their feelings, it's these two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T09:55:34-08:00","id":780595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=780506#post780506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, Legend 8 for Pan is really low. Ragnar\u00f6k has write-ups for gods like Forsetti or Bragi, and design them as viable parents, but there's no way Pan should be less 'famous' than them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, he is after all &quot;THE GREAT GOD PAN!&quot; He really ought to be high enough to rate breeding Scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T10:10:06-08:00","id":781184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=780498#post780498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What's even more confusing is his backstory says he's a god, yet his Legend is 8, which implies he's a demigod. I suppose it could have dropped after he left the Dodekatheon, but unlike them, he stayed behind in the world and took the form of Satan, so he's had thousands of years to rebuild his power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pan's backstory in Demigod is also highly flawed. The origin of his Satanic nature rightfully belongs to a more obscure mythical figure. The satyr Marsyas was the one who challenged Apollo to the contest, only to be flayed for his hubris. I have generally concluded that Pan's name was assigned to the role of Marsyas in Scion: Demigod so that they could have a more famous mythical figure covered rather than giving such a position to a comparatively minor one. In my games, though I have sometimes used it as written, I generally treat Pan as a full god in his own right (with Purviews such as Animal (Goat), Chaos, and Fertility favored) with his own Scions running around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T11:48:43-08:00","id":781223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/777740-can-pan-have-scions?p=781184#post781184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pan's backstory in Demigod is also highly flawed. The origin of his Satanic nature rightfully belongs to a more obscure mythical figure. The satyr Marsyas was the one who challenged Apollo to the contest, only to be flayed for his hubris. I have generally concluded that Pan's name was assigned to the role of Marsyas in Scion: Demigod so that they could have a more famous mythical figure covered rather than giving such a position to a comparatively minor one. In my games, though I have sometimes used it as written, I generally treat Pan as a full god in his own right (with Purviews such as Animal (Goat), Chaos, and Fertility favored) with his own Scions running around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw the Pan/Marsyas mix-up from the start. And I like the Idea of having Pan be a full God and Marsyas be the Satan impersonater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-06-2015, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}